  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 124 AM MST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nDaytime temperatures will run several degrees warmer than \nyesterday's, reaching around 5 to 10 degrees above climatological \nnorms. These above normal temperatures will persist throughout the \nentirety of the week, with many low-elevation areas reaching 60 \ndegrees for much of the period. A couple of weak shortwaves are \nstill expected to work through today and late Monday/early Tuesday. \nWith precipitation largely remaining north of our CWA, the main \nimpacts will be breezy winds and a few degree loss on our daytime \ntemps Tuesday. 500mb ensemble clusters still suggest differences \namongst models regarding the upper-level pattern come late \nweek/weekend. The National Blend now holds off introducing any PoPs \nuntil Friday afternoon, with chances increasing areawide through \nnext Monday.",
